      "stem": {
        "text": "Simplify $\\sqrt{50x^2y^3z}$, taking x and y to be positive.",
        "inline": []
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$5xy\\sqrt{2z}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$5\\sqrt{2xyz}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$10xy\\sqrt{z}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$25x^2y^2\\sqrt{z}$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": {
        "text": "Split the radicand into factors and pull out the squares: $\\sqrt{50x^2y^3z} = \\sqrt{25x^2y^2} \\sqrt{2yz} = 5xy\\sqrt{2yz}$.",
        "inline": []
